; natural numbers
;
; covers: `Nat` membership (0 is a natural number, and the successor of any natural number is
; a natural number) and the induction principle (a property true at 0 and preserved by
; successor is true of every natural number) -- see proofs/natural-numbers/induction.kurt for
; a worked example, including the "state base case and step as one conjunction" pattern
; `impl_elim`'s single-hop derivation needs to apply "induction" in one step.
;
; known gap: no arithmetic on `Nat` at all -- `+` is declared syntactically below (needed so
; `nat-succ`/"induction" can even parse `$n+1`) but has no defining axioms relating it to
; anything else (no `$n+0=$n`, no recursive step). This is a different, unrelated `+` from
; arith.kurt's: that one computes on literal numbers via `calc`, this one has no semantics of
; its own yet -- extending it (e.g. `$n + 0 = $n`, `$n + ($m+1) = ($n+$m)+1`) is real,
; self-contained future work.
load set

;; syntax
; `+` must bind tighter than `set.kurt`'s `in`/`∈` (25), otherwise `$n+1 in Nat` parses as
; `$n + (1 in Nat)` instead of `($n+1) in Nat`
infix + 60 60

;; inference rules
const Nat

use 0 in Nat  "nat-zero"
use $n in Nat  implies  $n+1 in Nat  "nat-succ"

; A(0)  and  forall n (A(n) -> A(n+1))   implies   forall n A(n)
use ((sub $x 0 %A) ∧ (∀ $n ∈ Nat  (sub $x $n %A  ⇒  sub $x ($n+1) %A)))   ⇒ ∀ $n in Nat  (sub $x $n %A)   "induction"

; for automatic testing we add the following line:
